# AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE Knowledge Base Mount

Treat the `AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` folder that sits next to this workspace, at `../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` (for example `.../Code/Local/AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE` on Windows and macOS), as a **mounted knowledge base** (**AGB**) for this workspace. Resolve it to an absolute path from the workspace root before reading. Read and apply its contents when planning, researching, or producing work here. Prefer its documents over inventing parallel structure.

**Abbreviation:** `AGB` = AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE. Use either form in conversation and artifacts; paths remain under the mount root below.

## Bootstrap (every session)

1. Read `AGB/AGENTS.md` first — authoritative orientation for all Type B agents.
2. Use `AGB/README.md` only as a short map if you need a directory overview.
3. Resolve paths below relative to the mount root above (absolute path). Do not assume files live inside AGENT-PLAYGROUND unless they actually do.

